sections.wikitext:
{{See also|Gone (Nelly song)}}
The official remix for "Dilemma" was produced by [[Jermaine Dupri]], and features Rowland and [[Ali (American rapper)|Ali]] of the [[St. Lunatics]]. It was included on Nelly's [[remix album]] titled ''[[Da Derrty Versions: The Reinvention]]'' (2003).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/da-derrty-versions-the-reinvention-mw0000321759|title=Da Derrty Versions: The Reinvention - Nelly|last=Birchmeier|first=Jason|publisher=AllMusic|access-date=April 29, 2020|archive-date=October 8, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211008122139/https://www.allmusic.com/album/da-derrty-versions-the-reinvention-mw0000321759|url-status=live}}</ref> Writing in a review for the album for RapReviews.com, Steve Juon criticized the [[bass guitar]] in the remix and stated that the song "should have been left alone",<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rapreviews.com/archive/2003_11_daderrty.html|title=Nelly :: Da Derrty Versions - The Reinvention :: Universal Records|last=Juon|first=Steve 'Flash'|publisher=RapReviews.com|date=November 25, 2003|access-date=October 15, 2021|archive-date=April 30, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230430083344/https://www.rapreviews.com/archive/2003_11_daderrty.html|url-status=live}}</ref> while Katharina Lobeck of [[BBC]] opined that the original song "worked better" and is "more coherent" than the remix.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/music/reviews/pqzf/|title=Da Derrty Versions: The Reinvention Review|last=Lobeck|first=Katharina|publisher=[[BBC]]|date=2004|access-date=October 15, 2021|archive-date=March 16, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210316152349/https://www.bbc.co.uk/music/reviews/pqzf/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On December 16, 2009, Nelly recorded a song titled "[[Gone (Nelly song)|Gone]]" with Rowland, which he initially dubbed as "Dilemma Part 2".<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.rap-up.com/2009/12/16/video-nelly-kelly-rowland-record-dilemma-sequel/|title=Video: Nelly & Kelly Rowland Record 'Dilemma' Sequel|website=[[Rap-Up]]|date=December 16, 2009|access-date=April 2, 2014|archive-date=August 23, 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100823203109/http://www.rap-up.com/2009/12/16/video-nelly-kelly-rowland-record-dilemma-sequel/|url-status=dead}}</ref> Nelly eventually retracted the statement, insisting that he did not want to replicate or diminish the original song but wanted to extend on the story and rekindle the chemistry he had with Rowland.<ref name="MTVGone">{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1648178/nelly-kelly-rowland-extend-story-dilemma-with-gone.jhtml|title=Nelly And Kelly Rowland 'Extend The Story' Of 'Dilemma' With 'Gone'|last=Rodriguez|first=Jayson|publisher=MTV News|date=September 17, 2010|access-date=April 29, 2020|archive-date=March 28, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140328105346/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1648178/nelly-kelly-rowland-extend-story-dilemma-with-gone.jhtml|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.stltoday.com/entertainment/music/kevin-johnson/nelly-releases-new-kelly-rowland-duet-gone/article_6264d432-23dc-11e0-a28c-0017a4a78c22.html|title=Nelly releases new Kelly Rowland duet "Gone"|last=Johnson|first=Kevin C.|website=[[St. Louis Post-Dispatch]]|date=January 19, 2011|access-date=April 29, 2020|archive-date=October 8, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211008122722/https://www.stltoday.com/entertainment/music/kevin-johnson/nelly-releases-new-kelly-rowland-duet-gone/article_6264d432-23dc-11e0-a28c-0017a4a78c22.html|url-status=live}}</ref> "Gone" was written by Nelly, [[Rico Love]], Earl Hood, Eric Goody II, and the producer [[Jim Jonsin]]. It was included on Nelly's sixth studio album ''[[5.0]]'' (2010),<ref name="MTVGone"/> and distributed to [[urban contemporary]] radio stations as its third single on January 4, 2011.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.allaccess.com/urban/future-releases|title=Future Adds: Urban/Urban AC|publisher=All Access|access-date=January 5, 2011|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110110011112/http://www.allaccess.com/urban/future-releases|archive-date=January 10, 2011}}</ref>

sections.text:
{{See also|Gone (Nelly song)}}
The official remix for "Dilemma" was produced by Jermaine Dupri, and features Rowland and Ali of the St. Lunatics. It was included on Nelly's remix album titled Da Derrty Versions: The Reinvention (2003). Writing in a review for the album for RapReviews.com, Steve Juon criticized the bass guitar in the remix and stated that the song "should have been left alone", while Katharina Lobeck of BBC opined that the original song "worked better" and is "more coherent" than the remix.

On December 16, 2009, Nelly recorded a song titled "Gone" with Rowland, which he initially dubbed as "Dilemma Part 2". Nelly eventually retracted the statement, insisting that he did not want to replicate or diminish the original song but wanted to extend on the story and rekindle the chemistry he had with Rowland. "Gone" was written by Nelly, Rico Love, Earl Hood, Eric Goody II, and the producer Jim Jonsin. It was included on Nelly's sixth studio album 5.0 (2010), and distributed to urban contemporary radio stations as its third single on January 4, 2011.

